ANGLE: keep every color attachment over depth/stencil fetch

Turnip offers 8 input attachments, as many as color attachments. To offer
GL_ARM_shader_framebuffer_fetch_depth_stencil ANGLE then cut the color
attachments and draw buffers to 6. Adreno's own driver offers 8 together
with depth/stencil fetch, and games written for it size their G-buffers
for 8: Wuthering Waves skips its velocity target with fewer and its frame
generation then reads a texture that was never made. Depth/stencil fetch
is now offered only where it fits beside every color attachment.

diff --git a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
index 38dddb9..4e328bc 100644
--- a/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/libANGLE/renderer/vulkan/vk_renderer.cpp
@@ -6700,6 +6700,12 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
     //
     // Additionally, the implementation assumes VK_KHR_dynamic_rendering_local_read to avoid
     // complications with VkRenderPass objects.
+    //
+    // Droidloom: only where depth and stencil fit beside every color attachment as input
+    // attachments.  Otherwise ANGLE would offer fewer color attachments than the device has, 6
+    // instead of 8 on Adreno with turnip, and games written for Adreno's own driver, which offers
+    // 8 together with depth/stencil fetch, drop render targets they still read.
+    const VkPhysicalDeviceLimits &limits = mPhysicalDeviceProperties.limits;
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(
         &mFeatures, supportsShaderFramebufferFetchDepthStencil,
         mFeatures.supportsShaderFramebufferFetch.enabled &&
@@ -6707,7 +6713,9 @@ void Renderer::initFeatures(const vk::ExtensionNameList &deviceExtensionNames,
                 VK_TRUE &&
             mRasterizationOrderAttachmentAccessFeatures.rasterizationOrderStencilAttachmentAccess ==
                 VK_TRUE &&
-            mFeatures.preferDynamicRendering.enabled);
+            mFeatures.preferDynamicRendering.enabled &&
+            std::min(limits.maxColorAttachments, limits.maxFragmentOutputAttachments) + 2 <=
+                limits.maxPerStageDescriptorInputAttachments);
 
     ANGLE_FEATURE_CONDITION(&mFeatures, supportsSynchronization2,
                             mSynchronization2Features.synchronization2 == VK_TRUE);
